<!--
    angr ITERegionConverter (angr/analyses/decompiler/optimization_passes/
    ite_region_converter.py, _find_ite_assignment_regions), S8 "goto-quality"
    sub-stage. decbench campaign feature F5, mined case
    O0-iproute2-ip-print_link_flags (GED 140 -> 11 with the option on).

    The option-gated ActionIteRegion (option `iteregion`, default-OFF; ELEM 4110)
    ports angr's ITERegionConverter: a source `?:` ternary compiles at -O0 to a
    two-arm register-assignment DIAMOND - one arm `mov eax, A`, the other
    `mov eax, B`, both converging on the use of the merged value. Ghidra/kuna's
    collapse-based structurer renders each diamond as a literal
    `if (c) { v = A } else { v = B }` statement pair, doubling the branch count of
    format/print/flag code (iproute2 print_link_flags: 41 ifs / 0 ternaries ->
    21 ifs / 20 ternaries when the diamonds collapse). The pass matches the narrow
    diamond (3-component BlockIf, single-CBRANCH condition, both clauses a single
    COPY to the SAME variable) and marks its CBRANCH; the S9 printer then emits
    `v = ( c ) ? A : B;` - Ghidra's printc has no ternary operator, so that emit
    hook is the one genuinely new piece. It is a PURELY print-time mark (no p-code
    cloned), so with the option off the pass never runs and output is
    byte-identical to upstream.

    *** RUNTIME CHOICE (why default-OFF and agent-flippable) ***
    An explicit source `if/else` compiles to the SAME object code as a `?:`
    ternary, so the diamond -> ternary rewrite matches the source ONLY when the
    source used a ternary. The binary cannot tell them apart, so this ships
    default-OFF and is flipped PER FUNCTION by an agent (`kuna catalog` ->
    `-option iteregion on`): ON for format/print/flag-heavy code where the ternary
    form dominates, OFF where explicit if/else is the likely source.

    Witness (self-contained, no relocations): a `-O0` function whose only body is a
    two-arm assignment diamond feeding a call -

        int pick(int x) { return use(x ? 0x10 : 0x20); }

    which compiles to `cmp x,0; je .else; mov eax,0x10; jmp .end;
    .else: mov eax,0x20; .end: mov edi,eax; call use`. The merged eax is used by
    the call, so the structurer keeps a real 3-component if/else BlockIf (not an
    early return), exactly the shape the pass inspects. The `use` callee resolves
    to an unnamed sub_401106 (outside the chunk), as in a stripped image.

    P0 assertion: `option iteregion on|off` (default off = upstream byte-identical).
    Pass 1 (option iteregion off): the diamond renders as a literal `if/else`
    (`else {`, the else-arm `= 0x10;`). Pass 2 (option iteregion on): the same
    diamond renders as the single ternary `v = (x == 0) ? 0x20 : 0x10;` and the
    rewrite is logged (`// ternary`). In both passes the merged variable
    still feeds the `sub_401106` call, proving the p-code is untouched.

    The `option ... off` preamble pins the pre-sweep (DIV-13 flags-off) structuring
    baseline (the same convention as ghangr-ifelseflatten.xml), so the canonical
    negated-guard `if (x == 0)` if/else diamond is what pass 1 sees and pass 2
    converts regardless of future default flips.
-->
